# HTML prototype standards

Apply when creating or editing `prototypes/<slug>/index.html`. Starters live
in the `design-prototype` skill's `templates/` folder.

## File

- One self-contained file: inline `<style>` and `<script>`, no external
  scripts, fonts, or network calls; inline SVG for icons.
- Version comment in `<head>`: prototype, slug, version, starter, states,
  changelog line.
- `index.html` is always the latest version; every version is also saved as
  `history/<version>.html`.

## Frame and states

- `#device` is a fixed 390×844 frame on desktop and fills the viewport on
  phones (`max-width: 430px`).
- `data-states` on `#device` lists every state id. `render(state)` derives the
  whole screen from the id, so `?state=<id>` is deterministic.
- `?capture=1` renders only the 390×844 frame: no review bar, no shadow, no
  motion. Export depends on it.
- The review bar ("State" switcher) sits outside `#device`.

## Safe areas

- Top: `max(env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px), 47px)`; bottom CTAs:
  `max(env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px), 34px)` plus spacing. Use `max()`, not a
  sum, so real devices are not double-padded.

## Touch and accessibility

- Touch targets 48px (meets 44pt iOS and 48dp Android).
- Semantic elements; visible `:focus-visible`; body text contrast at least WCAG AA.
- Sheets and dialogs: opacity-faded backdrop (no `hidden`), `inert` when
  closed, background `inert` when open, Escape closes, focus moves in and
  returns to the opener.
- Use the `hidden` attribute for whole views; the base CSS forces
  `[hidden] { display: none !important; }`.

## Style

- System font stack unless the brief names brand fonts.
- Tokens in `:root`; change values, keep names stable across iterations.
- Label placeholder copy in `notes.md` open questions.

## Do not

- Desktop-first layouts or breakpoints above 390px as the primary target.
- CDN frameworks (React, Tailwind) unless the designer asks.
- Remove the state scaffold or capture CSS.
